---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy of this Irish salary calculator 2026" description="Your gross pay, tax credits and PRSI class never leave your browser. Google Analytics audience cookies, no advertising, cookieless stability checks, and your rights.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-4 pb-8 prose prose-slate">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 17 October 2026</em></p>
    <p>
      irishnetpay.com is published by {LEGAL.entityName}. This policy explains, under the General Data Protection
      Regulation (GDPR) and Ireland’s Data Protection Act 2018, what happens to information about your visit. Put
      simply: what you type stays in your browser, the site shows no advertising, and the only cookies are those of
      Google Analytics audience measurement.
    </p>

    <h2>Figures you enter</h2>
    <p>
      Gross salary, pay frequency, tax credits, marital status, PRSI class, pension contributions or welfare
      details: everything you type to work out take-home pay, income tax, USC, PRSI or a social welfare payment is
      calculated by JavaScript on your own device. It is not sent to any server, not written to a database and not
      saved on your device either; closing the tab clears it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      What you type in the calculators is never stored in your browser. The only cookies are those of
      Google Analytics audience measurement, described below; there is no advertising cookie and no social media
      cookie. The site carries no advertising.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Tell visitors apart with a random identifier</td><td>13 months at most (390 days)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Keep the state of the current visit</td><td>13 months at most (390 days)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>These lifetimes are not extended on each visit; Google’s default is 2 years and the site shortens it.</p>

    <h2>Audience measurement with Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are useful: pages viewed, referring page,
      visit length, device and browser type, approximate country and city. The IP address is anonymised: Google
      Analytics 4 neither logs nor stores it. The page address sent to Google is stripped of its parameters, so the
      figures you enter are never included. Ad storage, ad user data, ad personalisation and Google signals are
      switched off, and measurement data is shared with no advertiser.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Processor</strong>: Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, acting on the publisher’s behalf (Article 28 GDPR). Data may be transferred to Google LLC in the United States under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.</li>
      <li><strong>Purpose</strong>: audience measurement.</li>
      <li><strong>Retention</strong>: 14 months for visit-level and identifier-level data, then deletion; only anonymous totals remain.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal basis</strong>: the publisher’s legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
      <li><strong>Objecting</strong>: block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. The calculators work exactly the same.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2>
    <p>
      To find what goes wrong (JavaScript errors, slow loading, buttons that do nothing when clicked, broken
      scrolling), the site uses <strong>Microsoft Clarity in cookieless mode</strong>. In this mode Clarity sets
      none of <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>; each page view has
      its own identifier, and separate page views or visits are never linked. Page text and every value typed into
      a field are masked in your browser before anything is sent, so Microsoft never sees your salary or your
      tax credits.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Controller</strong>: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, which may process the data in the United States under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses (<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Purpose</strong>: a technical, anonymous check that the pay and welfare calculators load and give results.</li>
      <li><strong>Retention</strong>: 30 days for page-view recordings, 13 months for aggregated figures.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal basis</strong>: the publisher’s legitimate interest in running calculators that work (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
      <li><strong>Objecting</strong>: block <code>clarity.ms</code> in your browser or content blocker (the calculators work exactly the same), or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.), whose servers log technical request data (IP address, time,
      page requested, browser) for security and to keep the service running. The publisher has no access to these
      logs and does not use them.
    </p>

    <h2>Emails</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, your message is used to reply and for
      nothing else; your address is not added to any list or shared.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      The GDPR gives you rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction and objection. With no user accounts, the
      publisher usually holds no data that identifies you; in practice they apply to any email you have sent and to
      audience measurement, and can also be exercised with Google or Microsoft. You may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}
      (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">how to contact the DPC</a>), or to
      the CNIL in France, where the publisher is established.
    </p>
    <p>See also the <a href="/legal/">legal notice</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
